{"id": "EUVD-2026-64568", "enisaUuid": "c6aba5cc-2bd2-30b5-a9e0-314419e2955b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: smc: fix splice entry lifetime imbalance in smc_rx_splice\n\nsmc_rx_splice() passes pages to splice_to_pipe() before taking the\nreferences that cover the lifetime of each splice entry. In the\nVM-backed RMB path, splice_to_pipe() may drop unqueued entries through\nsmc_rx_spd_release(), while queued entries are released later via the\npipe buffer callback.\n\nThe old post-splice accounting also derives the number of queued VM pages\nfrom an offset mutated while building the descriptor, and a multi-page\nsplice pairs one sock_hold() with multiple sock_put() calls.\n\nTake the page and socket references for every candidate entry before\nsplice_to_pipe(), and drop the matching private state, page reference,\nand socket reference from smc_rx_spd_release() for entries that never\nget queued. This fixes a refcount imbalance that can underflow page\nrefcounts and trigger a use-after-free.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:32:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:06:03", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ddc7af2ae7fc5a0c0635b245c0824c8b76de5cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07ad246529d136d5ef441d5ab4c305d132ff3090", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c841789e456ec6751342fa800639ce8e82ff0e6b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af02c67ce654356c58db20a0bb2db33ace3b07a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca8342b5fc24c249fdb998468f6a168b457c67e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b7d54cedea5cb158e21925ae0c6c2f5c87ed2a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4515c78f4d9fd577270f012efeb062ea58b3682d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d9686af2976741bbd79b150d1c9e60b81e7f12e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-75cj-q634-phhq", "CVE-2026-74631"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cf1d5a1-ac95-309d-8abb-9712dcbada00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.104"}, {"id": "15eab7a2-3604-302f-8acc-576e89fbb98d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9014db202cb764b8e14c53e7bacc81f9a1a2ba7f <af02c67ce654356c58db20a0bb2db33ace3b07a8"}, {"id": "20d091e8-9c45-3b18-9659-1b97b292adfa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9014db202cb764b8e14c53e7bacc81f9a1a2ba7f <c841789e456ec6751342fa800639ce8e82ff0e6b"}, {"id": "4ae18121-75fc-3b89-802b-1e1e27acfc87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9014db202cb764b8e14c53e7bacc81f9a1a2ba7f <07ad246529d136d5ef441d5ab4c305d132ff3090"}, {"id": "4faffd3c-4664-3110-8ed5-0c4b3a268d5f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9014db202cb764b8e14c53e7bacc81f9a1a2ba7f <ca8342b5fc24c249fdb998468f6a168b457c67e5"}, {"id": "5d0bebf1-e603-3992-9dd1-1efeda4eec6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.217"}, {"id": "5ef2be77-34e7-3838-88cc-528178fabd0a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9014db202cb764b8e14c53e7bacc81f9a1a2ba7f <5d9686af2976741bbd79b150d1c9e60b81e7f12e"}, {"id": "671c1674-d4bb-3d80-8cd6-dc6d6e9fcff6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9014db202cb764b8e14c53e7bacc81f9a1a2ba7f <0b7d54cedea5cb158e21925ae0c6c2f5c87ed2a0"}, {"id": "685062b1-27c0-399e-a825-430cba01136a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.266"}, {"id": "77302b57-8636-30d2-a3a8-fbaef76a488b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}, {"id": "7ecf6874-fd21-33a7-961c-01b89ef8fd48", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9014db202cb764b8e14c53e7bacc81f9a1a